BOOKMARKS
=========

Aquí tienes el archivo completo en texto plano para que lo puedas copiar y pegar directamente:

- https://pll.harvard.edu/course/cs50-introduction-computer-science — Introductory Harvard course covering core computer science concepts and programming fundamentals #cs #intro #learning
- https://teachyourselfcs.com — Structured self-study roadmap to learn computer science fundamentals independently #cs #roadmap
- https://sarabander.github.io/sicp/html/index.xhtml — Online version of Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs (SICP) #cs #books #theory
- https://softwarefoundations.cis.upenn.edu — Interactive series on logic, formal verification, and programming language theory #cs #books #theory #math
- https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu — Complete Feynman Lectures on Physics covering fundamental physics concepts #physics #science
- https://www.nand2tetris.org — Hands-on course building a computer system from logic gates to high-level software #cs #hardware #learning
- https://missing.csail.mit.edu — Practical guide to essential developer tools like shell, git, and scripting #tools #cli #git
- https://craftinginterpreters.com — Step-by-step guide to building interpreters and programming languages #compilers #books #architecture
- https://aalhour.com/awesome-compilers — Curated list of compiler design resources and tools #compilers #resources
- https://www.cprogramming.com — Tutorials and references for learning C and C++ programming #cpp #c #learning
- https://seenaburns.com/building-c-programs — Guide to compiling and structuring C programs #c #compilers #tools
- https://learn-c.org — Free interactive C tutorial and practice from the browser #c #learning #interactive
